 "notes": [
  [
   "SAO++ power select: the switch common (VLOAD) feeds the four '+' wire pads on the timer. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell.",
   [
    38.1,
    35.56
   ]
  ],
  [
   "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other.",
   [
    38.1,
    39.37
   ]
  ],
  [
   "LED-only board: SDA, SCL, GPIO1 and GPIO2 are not connected, so no series diode is needed on the cell (see docs/standard.md section 3).",
   [
    38.1,
    43.18
   ]
  ],
  [
   "J2..J9 are bare 1.6 mm copper pads on the front (nothing to buy). NorthSec's original had 0.7 mm plated holes for the same eight points.",
   [
    38.1,
    137.16
   ]
  ],
  [
   "The game: each LED circuit is open until the builder solders a jumper wire from any '+' pad to that LED's numbered pad. Cut a wire and its LED goes out.",
   [
    38.1,
    140.97
   ]
  ],
  [
   "Pad 1 (J3) -> R1 -> D1 upper left, pad 2 (J7) -> R3 -> D3 upper right, pad 3 (J5) -> R2 -> D2 lower left, pad 4 (J9) -> R4 -> D4 lower right (front view), the pairing NorthSec used.",
   [
    38.1,
    144.78
   ]
  ],
  [
   "A wire can only ever join VLOAD to a resistor, so no wiring mistake between these pads can short the supply or reach the coin cell.",
   [
    38.1,
    148.59
   ]
  ],
  [
   "1.3 k gives about 1 mA per red LED from the cell and about 1.2 mA from the badge (NorthSec used 330 ohm on 3.3 V, about 4 mA).",
   [
    38.1,
    152.4
   ]
  ]
 ]
}